Narrow Rust DOCX semantics port derived from Hermes Agent:
https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
Revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899
Source: tools/read_extract.py::_extract_docx, _joined, _open_zip, _zip_xml.

Retained behavior: transitional WordprocessingML paragraph/run text in document
order, tab/break/carriage-return text, and ruby phonetic-guide exclusion.
Local changes: portable byte-only Rust API, streaming namespace-aware XML,
closed versioned results, exact source paragraph ordinals, explicit main-body
coverage, fields/deletions/drawing/textbox exclusions, bounded ZIP/XML expansion,
entry/path/overlap/encryption/ZIP64/multi-disk policy, checked CRC/size, and
whole-paragraph text limits only after complete selected XML validation.
rawzip performs ZIP parsing; fixed unsupported-format policy comparisons use
only offsets supplied by the checked library because its public API omits the
EOCD disk fields. No Python runtime, broad converter dispatch, network/OCR,
installation/self-repair, upstream tests, or private Hermes files are included.
The local test fixtures and assertions were independently authored.

